      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T04:40:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`boot_to_type` at line 513 stages the one-time boot: `boot_to` calls `clear_job_queue`, then `send_one_time_boot`, then creates the BIOS config job (`external/badfish.py:1104-1111`). If `_apply_bootmode` fails once here, `_apply_bootmode_with_retry` calls `_clear_bootmode_jobs`, which deletes that job, then retries. The retry can return True after a recovered read or a set, and the code reboots without running `boot_to_type` again, so the PXE override is gone. I reproduced the order with stubbed dispatchers: `boot_to_type` -\u003e `clear_job_queue` -\u003e `reboot`. Suggest calling plain `_apply_bootmode` here (the mode was already reconciled in `prepare_host_hardware`), or re-running `boot_to_type` after any clear.",
      "revId": "168f0aa38b051f31b558822ead1efb811f1ebd48",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
